# Adding a lint rule

Use `AnalysisRule` / `MultiAnalysisRule` + `registerNodeProcessors`. Report with `rule.reportAtNode(node, diagnosticCode: ...)`.
Do not use `custom_lint_builder` or `DartLintRule`.

## One rule per diagnostic name

Each user-facing diagnostic name is one rule class extending `ArchitectureImportRule`, and the rule's `name` must equal that diagnostic name: the analyzer only runs a rule when the diagnostic named after `rule.name` is enabled, so sharing one rule across names makes them depend on each other. Subclasses only implement `diagnosticCodeFor(currentLayer, importedLayer)`; the base class visits imports and exports and resolves the layers.

A new message variant of an existing diagnostic is a new `LintCodeArchitecture` (same name, unique `uniqueName`) listed in that rule's `diagnosticCodes`.

Reuse the helpers in `import_resolver.dart` (`layerOf`, `isSameProject`, `isThirdPartyPackage`, `importedUriOf`, `exportedUriOf`).
Work with the analyzer's resolved URIs (`node.libraryImport`, `node.libraryExport`, `context.currentUnit?.unit.declaredFragment?.source.uri`), not file-system paths.

## After changing diagnostics

1. `registry.registerLintRule(...)` and export from `lib/clean_arch_lint.dart` if you added a class
2. Enable the diagnostic name in `example/analysis_options.yaml` under `plugins.clean_arch_lint.diagnostics`
3. Violations in `example/lib/{layer}/bad_example_*.dart` (CI fails unless each one is reported), listed in `example/README.md`
4. Rule tests in `test/rules_test.dart` (`AnalysisRuleTest` from `analyzer_testing`) for every new diagnostic case, plus `test/import_resolver_test.dart` for new resolver behavior
5. Dartdoc on the rule / `LintCode` (severity, violation, yaml)
6. README.md, USAGE.md, RULES.md, CHANGELOG.md, and the library dartdoc in `lib/clean_arch_lint.dart`

```dart
@override
FutureOr<void> register(PluginRegistry registry) {
  registry.registerLintRule(NoDataDependenciesRule());
  registry.registerLintRule(NoScreensDependenciesRule());
  registry.registerLintRule(DomainOnlyDependsOnItselfRule());
  registry.registerLintRule(AllowThirdPartyPackagesInDomainRule());
}
```
